-- 0879 · The club demo: the community member finds a full, lived-in app, with a shop (owner request 2026-10-16: "fill up all spots that we can fill with test data").
--
-- Pack demo_neutral_club_v1 goes to version 3. The persona is Kwame Osei (the family's main adult; Abena is his wife, Kofi 15 is their son). Same idea as 0878 for the
-- faith demo, in a neighborhood club's words. Every row is invented: names obviously fictional, phones 555-01xx, e-mails on demo.weaverams.org, links to a
-- placeholder address on a domain nobody owns.
--
--   Modules    The pack now names "store" and "niva" (center.modules): app.demo_align_center grants what the pack names, so the club has its shop and its assistant
--              (Weaver's grant, no person involved), and the store lead, the pickup volunteer and the kitchen lead have their work from the first reset (the
--              2 orders and 2 low-stock items the pack already had were invisible while the shop was off). A reset keeps the grants, as it did before.
--   Money      Two pledges and three payments of the Osei family, in whole cents: the annual appeal ($150.00) paid in full by a test-mode card payment, and a raised
--              garden bed ($300.00) paid in part ($100.00 by Zelle, $50.00 by check), with receipts. Their open pledge is untouched: the $125.00 garden pledge is still
--              open with no payment against it (an unmatched $125.00 Zelle bank line waits for it), and the part-paid pledge is NEWER than it, so the pledge the demo
--              hangs a waiting payment confirmation on (0877: the family's oldest open pledge with at least $25.00 open) is the same as before. Five things to give to
--              (Raised garden bed, Tool shed with three choices, Seed and soil kit, Any amount for the garden, Sponsor a potluck) and a monthly gift of $20.00 that
--              waits for a card and is never charged.
--   Store      Two orders of the family: one picked up last time, one placed for the next pickup (items that are not counted on the shelf).
--   Events     The clean-up day gets lunch in four lunch times and a small contribution on the RSVP; a garden work morning tomorrow (36 hours' notice, so "Still coming?"
--              waits for the family all day); the family attended the last potluck.
--   Calendar   Two layers (club events, garden crew), entries for every published event and the garden days; two photo albums (links); an event-feedback form for
--              the last potluck (open) and an open poll, with a few answers.
--   Guide      Times and visiting, Links, Membership; a question the office answered and closed; the committee lists; library texts the assistant answers from.
--   Family     Three special days, profile details with an emergency contact, the family's member numbers, and that both adults may vote.
--
-- NOT HERE, AND WHY. Statements, photos, videos and audio (files in storage) cannot be loaded by a pack. The club has no school, so it has no Learning Center rows.
--
-- THE LIVE DEMO. As in 0878: the running club reloads the new version by itself (0877) or with Start over, and this migration aligns it now (the shop and the assistant
-- are granted at once) and writes one audit entry ("demo.pack_updated") for every club demo still on an older pack.

